{
  "analysis": "We need to solve Codeforces problem 820D: given a permutation p of length n, among all cyclic right shifts of p, find the shift that minimizes the deviation defined by sum_i |i - q_i| where q is the shifted permutation. A direct brute force would be O(n^2). The trick is to express the deviation for a shift k in O(log n) time per k by sweeping k and maintaining two multisets of values a_i = p_i - i, splitting the indices into two parts that depend on the current shift. Let t = n - k (1 <= t <= n). Then the deviation F(t) can be written as: F(t) = sum_{j=1..t} |a_j - k| + sum_{j=t+1..n} |a_j + t|, where k = n - t. As t varies from 1 to n, the first sum uses the threshold A = k, and the second sum uses threshold B = -t. We can compute both sums efficiently with two Fenwick trees (ordered by value of a_j) that keep counts and sums for the two active sets: T1 = {a_1..a_t} and T2 = {a_{t+1}..a_n}. For a threshold X, sum_{x in set} |x - X| equals (X * count_le - sum_le) + ((total_sum - sum_le) - X * (total_count - count_le)), where count_le and sum_le are the number of elements <= X and the sum of those elements in the current set. We sweep t from 1 to n, update the two Fenwicks by moving a_{t+1} from T2 to T1, and compute F(t) using the current totals. We track the minimum F and corresponding shift k = n - t. This runs in O(n log n) time and O(n) memory, suitable for n up to 1e6. The implementation uses 64-bit integers for safety.",
  "plan": "1) Implement a C++17 program that reads n and p. Compute a[i] = p[i] - i. 2) Prepare two Fenwick trees (for counts and sums) for T1 and T2 over the value domain of a, which lies in [-(n-1), (n-1)]. 3) Initialize T1 with a[1] and T2 with a[2..n]. Maintain total counts and sums for both sets. 4) For t from 1 to n, compute F(t) using thresholds A = n - t (for T1) and B = -t (for T2) via Fenwick queries. 5) Move a[t+1] from T2 to T1 and update totals when t < n. 6) Keep the minimum F and corresponding best_t, output F and shift k = n - best_t. 7) Provide a small test with sample inputs to verify correctness.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp << 'CPP'
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

struct Fenwick {
    int n;
    vector<long long> bit;
    Fenwick(int n_ = 0) { init(n_); }
    void init(int n_) { n = n_; bit.assign(n + 1, 0); }
    void add(int idx, long long val) {
        for (int i = idx; i <= n; i += i & -i) bit[i] += val;
    }
    long long sum(int idx) const {
        long long res = 0;
        for (int i = idx; i > 0; i -= i & -i) res += bit[i];
        return res;
    }
};

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int n; 
    if (!(cin >> n)) return 0;
    vector<int> p(n + 1);
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) cin >> p[i];
    vector<int> a(n + 1);
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) a[i] = p[i] - i;

    int M = 2 * n - 1;            // domain size for a: [-(n-1), (n-1)]
    int minV = -(n - 1);

    Fenwick cnt1(M), sum1(M), cnt2(M), sum2(M);
    auto idxVal = [&](int x) { return x + n; }; // maps value x in [-(n-1), n-1] to [1, 2n-1]

    long long total_sum1 = 0, total_sum2 = 0;
    int total_count1 = 0, total_count2 = 0;

    // Initialize: t = 1 -> T1 has a[1], T2 has a[2..n]
    total_count1 = 1;
    total_sum1 = a[1];
    int id0 = idxVal(a[1]);
    cnt1.add(id0, 1);
    sum1.add(id0, a[1]);

    total_count2 = n - 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {
        int id = idxVal(a[i]);
        cnt2.add(id, 1);
        sum2.add(id, a[i]);
        total_sum2 += a[i];
    }

    long long bestF = LLONG_MAX;
    int best_t = 1;

    for (int t = 1; t <= n; ++t) {
        int A = n - t;            // threshold for T1
        int idxA = A + n;
        long long count_le1 = cnt1.sum(idxA);
        long long sum_le1 = sum1.sum(idxA);
        long long f1 = 1LL * A * count_le1 - sum_le1 + (total_sum1 - sum_le1) - 1LL * A * (total_count1 - count_le1);

        int B = -t;                   // threshold for T2
        long long count_le2 = 0, sum_le2 = 0;
        if (B < minV) {
            count_le2 = 0; sum_le2 = 0;
        } else if (B >= (n - 1)) {
            count_le2 = total_count2; sum_le2 = total_sum2;
        } else {
            int idxB = B + n;
            count_le2 = cnt2.sum(idxB);
            sum_le2 = sum2.sum(idxB);
        }
        long long f2 = 1LL * B * count_le2 - sum_le2 + (total_sum2 - sum_le2) - 1LL * B * (total_count2 - count_le2);

        long long F = f1 + f2;
        if (F < bestF) {
            bestF = F;
            best_t = t;
        }

        if (t < n) {
            int toMove = a[t + 1];
            int idMove = idxVal(toMove);
            cnt1.add(idMove, 1);
            sum1.add(idMove, toMove);
            total_count1 += 1;
            total_sum1 += toMove;

            cnt2.add(idMove, -1);
            sum2.add(idMove, -toMove);
            total_count2 -= 1;
            total_sum2 -= toMove;
        }
    }

    int best_k = n - best_t;
    cout << bestF << " " << best_k << "\n";
    return 0;
}
