  "plan": "1) Create a self-contained Python script detect_encoding.py that can detect encoding of given bytes. It will: - try chardet.detect(data) if chardet is available - otherwise fall back to attempting UTF-8 decode, and finally latin-1 as a fallback. 2) Make the script executable. 3) Create test files to exercise the detector: a UTF-8 text file and a binary file that is not valid UTF-8. 4) Run the detector against those test files and observe outputs. 5) Optionally install chardet for improved accuracy if network access is available.",
  "commands": [
